WEBVTT

00:00.473 --> 00:03.822
♪ It seems today
that all you see ♪

00:03.922 --> 00:07.190
♪ Is violence in movies
and sex on TV ♪

00:07.225 --> 00:10.760
♪ But where are those
good old-fashioned values ♪

00:10.796 --> 00:13.763
♪ On which we used to rely? ♪

00:13.799 --> 00:17.267
♪ Lucky there's a family guy ♪

00:17.302 --> 00:20.570
♪ Lucky there's a man
who positively can do ♪

00:20.605 --> 00:22.138
♪ All the things that make us ♪

00:22.174 --> 00:23.506
♪ Laugh and cry ♪

00:23.542 --> 00:24.080
♪ He's... a...
Fam... ily... Guy! ♪

00:34.086 --> 00:36.252
Where are you going?

00:36.288 --> 00:38.154
I'm going to Quagmire's
to get some hand-me-downs.

00:38.190 --> 00:40.957
His dad-mom sent over
some boxes of men's clothes

00:40.993 --> 00:43.360
from back before the ol'
chippety-choppety.

00:43.395 --> 00:45.729
You shouldn't wear
people's old, dirty clothes.

00:45.764 --> 00:47.163
Well, I'm a dirty guy, Lois.

00:47.199 --> 00:48.732
Haven't you ever seen
my naughty,

00:48.767 --> 00:50.800
late-night, party-line
commercials?

00:50.836 --> 00:53.003
Hey, are you lonely?

00:53.038 --> 00:55.739
Do you like to party
with hot girls?

00:55.774 --> 00:59.209
What about horsing around
with fat guys?

00:59.244 --> 01:00.844
Well, what are you
waiting for?

01:00.879 --> 01:02.879
Give us a call.

01:02.914 --> 01:04.914
I'll be on the toilet,
wearing a T-shirt

01:04.950 --> 01:06.916
that's so long
I have to hold it

01:06.952 --> 01:09.419
under my chin
while I wipe.

01:14.192 --> 01:17.427
Wow, your dad doesn't
use this Dickie anymore?

01:17.462 --> 01:18.762
That's crazy.

01:18.797 --> 01:21.531
Why would anyone get rid
of a perfectly good Dickie?

01:21.566 --> 01:23.600
I see what you're doing,
and cut it out.

01:23.635 --> 01:25.201
Hey, what are these?

01:27.205 --> 01:29.506
Oh, my God, I haven't
seen these in years!

01:29.541 --> 01:30.541
What do you got there?

01:30.575 --> 01:32.108
Some kind of home movie
from the Orient?

01:32.144 --> 01:33.777
<i>No, no, this is
Winter Summer.</i>

01:33.812 --> 01:35.845
It was a Korean soap opera
that I was in.

01:35.881 --> 01:37.747
You were in a
Korean soap opera?

01:37.783 --> 01:39.883
Yeah, back when the Navy
had me stationed in Busan,

01:39.918 --> 01:42.218
I saw an ad in the paper
for guys over five-foot-four,

01:42.254 --> 01:44.054
and I was the only one
who showed up.

01:44.089 --> 01:45.488
Next thing I know,
I'm on TV,

01:45.524 --> 01:47.457
playing a guy
named American Johnny.

01:47.492 --> 01:49.559
Wow, I didn't even
know you could act.

01:49.594 --> 01:51.528
You also didn't know
I was a rock polisher.

01:51.563 --> 01:52.629
Take a look at that.

01:52.664 --> 01:54.130
Oh, my! What is that?

01:54.166 --> 01:55.498
That's tiger eye.

01:55.534 --> 01:57.767
Extraordinary.

02:34.439 --> 02:36.172
Holy crap, Quagmire,
you speak Korean?

02:36.208 --> 02:37.474
Nah, not really.

02:37.509 --> 02:39.275
They just told me how to sound
the words out phonetically.

02:39.311 --> 02:41.444
So you never knew what
you were actually saying?

02:41.480 --> 02:43.613
No. In fact,
at the height of the show,

02:43.648 --> 02:45.849
I did a whole
pro-genital-mutilation PSA

02:45.884 --> 02:48.351
that I really regret.

02:48.386 --> 02:49.352
Wow, that girl's hot.

02:49.387 --> 02:50.353
That's a guy.

02:50.388 --> 02:51.354
That other guy's handsome.

02:51.389 --> 02:52.355
That's a girl.

02:52.390 --> 02:53.356
That cat is cute.

02:53.391 --> 02:54.357
That's a dog.

02:54.392 --> 02:56.259
What is everything?!

02:58.063 --> 03:00.263
Oh, my God,
if Hee-Sun and Bong-Hwa

03:00.298 --> 03:02.499
don't get together,
I'm gonna kill myself!

03:02.534 --> 03:03.666
You're crazy!

03:03.702 --> 03:05.335
Bong-Hwa is completely
dishonorable!

03:05.370 --> 03:08.538
He brought a personal
item to work!

03:23.822 --> 03:25.388
Oh, my God!
No way!

03:25.423 --> 03:27.056
I told you!
I told you!

03:27.092 --> 03:30.527
Wow, I guess he didn't die
in the vending machine.

03:30.562 --> 03:32.562
♪ ♪

03:36.701 --> 03:37.701
What?! It's over?!

03:37.736 --> 03:39.235
Should we put in
the next one?

03:39.271 --> 03:40.303
Of course we should.

03:40.338 --> 03:41.905
We are binge-watching
this whole show.

03:41.940 --> 03:43.580
I mean, I haven't been
this into something

03:43.608 --> 03:45.408
<i>since The Shawshank Redemption.</i>

03:45.443 --> 03:47.744
Yes, um, after you escaped
into the hole,

03:47.779 --> 03:51.080
how did you perfectly re-attach
the Raquel Welch poster

03:51.116 --> 03:53.183
from inside the hole
with a tautness

03:53.218 --> 03:54.484
that a rock could pierce?

03:54.519 --> 03:55.785
Does it really matter?

03:55.820 --> 03:56.786
It does to me.

03:56.821 --> 03:58.288
Did you even
like the movie?

03:58.323 --> 04:00.690
I did very much
up until that point.

04:41.933 --> 04:44.901
♪ ♪

04:44.936 --> 04:46.336
Oh, my God!

04:46.371 --> 04:47.870
Quagmire, give me the last tape!

04:47.906 --> 04:49.606
Huh. Sorry, guys.

04:49.641 --> 04:51.040
There are no more tapes.

04:51.076 --> 04:53.042
What?!
Where's the last one?!

04:53.078 --> 04:54.078
He's right.

04:54.112 --> 04:55.979
Oh, my God!
What do we do?!

04:56.014 --> 04:57.280
Quagmire, tell us
what happened!

04:57.315 --> 04:58.915
Did Hee-Sun live
to have the baby?!

04:58.950 --> 05:01.517
Did Kim secure a position
at the hydroelectric plant?!

05:01.553 --> 05:03.086
I don't know.
I don't remember.

05:03.121 --> 05:04.721
How can you
not remember?

05:04.756 --> 05:05.855
It was 20 years ago.

05:05.890 --> 05:06.956
We shot out of order.

05:06.992 --> 05:08.725
I-I never even knew
what I was saying.

05:08.760 --> 05:10.526
I didn't care.
I was living the life.

05:10.562 --> 05:12.895
Just banging chicks
and eating cabbage, you know.

05:12.931 --> 05:15.231
Aw, crap, what do we do
about our show?

05:15.267 --> 05:18.101
Now I know how that German
movie producer felt.

05:18.136 --> 05:20.570
All right, Friedrich,
now that World War Two is over,

05:20.605 --> 05:22.639
we can get back
to making comedies again.

05:22.674 --> 05:24.741
Get me these comedy writers.

05:24.776 --> 05:27.777
Uh... I don't think any of
these guys are available.

05:27.812 --> 05:29.078
What?! This is terrible!

05:29.114 --> 05:30.513
Get me my agent!

05:30.548 --> 05:33.349
He's, uh, he's probably
not gonna answer either.

05:33.385 --> 05:35.051
Well, this is crazy!
What happened...?

05:35.086 --> 05:37.920
Oh, I remember what happened.

05:41.826 --> 05:44.027
That episode's
not online anywhere.

05:44.062 --> 05:46.896
I even tried the Korean
search engine Bing Bong.

05:46.931 --> 05:48.431
That's not real.

05:48.466 --> 05:49.799
All right, it's not,
but, Quagmire,

05:49.834 --> 05:50.900
we need that episode.

05:50.935 --> 05:52.435
We got to know what happened!

05:52.470 --> 05:54.237
Guys, I'm sorry,
but it was years ago,

05:54.272 --> 05:56.105
and it never aired
outside Korea.

05:56.141 --> 05:59.242
So... we go to Korea.

05:59.277 --> 06:00.510
Yes.
Buying tickets.

06:00.545 --> 06:01.611
Come on, guys,

06:01.646 --> 06:03.646
it's just a dumb,
forgotten TV show.

06:03.682 --> 06:06.382
<i>Quagmire, we have to know
how Winter Summer ends.</i>

06:06.418 --> 06:08.618
This show is our
whole life now.

06:08.653 --> 06:10.887
Yeah, if we don't find
that tape, we're screwed.

06:10.922 --> 06:14.157
Like anybody who goes
scuba diving with Dave Navarro.

06:38.049 --> 06:41.117
All right, gang, me and the
guys are off to Korea to find

06:41.152 --> 06:44.153
the last episode of a soap
opera Quagmire was in.

06:44.189 --> 06:45.688
Peter, this is ridiculous.

06:45.724 --> 06:47.657
Wh-What am I supposed to do
if work calls?

06:47.692 --> 06:49.025
Just do what I do.

06:49.060 --> 06:51.861
<i>Hold the phone up to any
episode of Who's the Boss?</i>

06:51.896 --> 06:53.162
Griffin, it's been four days.

06:53.198 --> 06:54.664
Why haven't you come to work?

06:54.699 --> 06:55.765
Angela?

06:55.800 --> 06:57.200
Of course it's me!

06:57.235 --> 06:59.402
You know, I've got half a mind
to fire you.

06:59.437 --> 07:00.937
Angela.

07:00.972 --> 07:03.306
Oh, I can't stay mad at you.

07:03.341 --> 07:05.842
I'll see you when I see you.

07:05.877 --> 07:09.445
♪ ♪

07:24.562 --> 07:28.131
Man, Epcot nailed Asia.

07:28.166 --> 07:31.033
American Johnny!

07:36.775 --> 07:39.575
Holy crap, Quagmire,
you're famous here!

07:39.611 --> 07:40.576
It's American Johnny!

07:40.612 --> 07:42.445
American Johnny is back!

07:42.480 --> 07:45.214
I take a picture with
giant Samsung phone!

07:45.250 --> 07:48.818
Giant Samsung phone
is also tiny Kia car!

08:00.174 --> 08:02.307
Welcome,
American Johnny.

08:02.343 --> 08:04.710
We give only
best room for you.

08:04.745 --> 08:06.945
Would you like smoking
or chain smoking?

08:06.981 --> 08:09.181
Uh, smoking, I guess?

08:09.216 --> 08:11.083
Yes, and how many
ridiculous things

08:11.118 --> 08:13.151
would you like
your toilet to do?

08:13.187 --> 08:15.821
Do you have one that goes,
"Yum-yum-yum-yum-yum"?

08:15.856 --> 08:18.390
Ah, presidential suite!

08:23.197 --> 08:25.063
Well, Donna's
mother died.

08:25.099 --> 08:27.032
But we should probably
head out to find

08:27.067 --> 08:29.034
the last episode of
that Korean soap opera.

08:29.069 --> 08:30.402
Yeah. Where's Peter?

08:30.437 --> 08:32.170
Oh, he went
to get plastic surgery.

08:32.206 --> 08:33.505
He did?

08:33.540 --> 08:35.540
Yeah, Korea's the plastic
surgery capital of the world.

08:35.576 --> 08:37.476
Nobody here thinks
you look good unless you have

08:37.511 --> 08:39.945
big, round eyes
and a tiny little nose and chin.

08:39.980 --> 08:40.946
Hey, guys.

08:40.981 --> 08:42.447
Peter, are you
all right?!

08:42.483 --> 08:43.916
You know what?
I feel good.

08:43.951 --> 08:46.051
I feel like I want
to giggle behind my hand

08:46.086 --> 08:48.387
at a lot of things
and hold, but not eat,

08:48.422 --> 08:50.088
a big ice cream cone.

08:55.129 --> 08:57.162
There were more birds
than videos in there.

08:57.197 --> 08:58.797
<i>Yeah, and no sign
of Winter Summer.</i>

08:58.832 --> 09:00.265
Glenn?

09:00.301 --> 09:01.700
Glenn Quagmire?

09:03.137 --> 09:04.369
Sujin?

09:10.911 --> 09:12.277
It's Hee-Sun!

09:12.313 --> 09:13.313
From the show!

09:13.347 --> 09:14.347
I don't believe it.

09:14.381 --> 09:15.580
She's so beautiful.

09:15.616 --> 09:17.316
She's so beautiful!

09:17.351 --> 09:18.717
H-How did you find me?

09:18.752 --> 09:20.419
I heard that American
Johnny was back,

09:20.454 --> 09:21.853
so I started
following you

09:21.889 --> 09:24.656
on the new "Where
American Johnny?" app.

09:24.692 --> 09:26.325
I already rich from that.

09:26.360 --> 09:28.293
Dance for me, Hilary Duff!

09:28.329 --> 09:29.795
♪ ♪

09:31.799 --> 09:33.532
Ah, it's so great
to see you, Sujin.

09:33.567 --> 09:35.734
You look just
as pretty as ever.

09:35.769 --> 09:38.971
I've waited every day
hoping you would return.

09:39.006 --> 09:41.273
And I never stopped
thinking of you.

09:42.309 --> 09:43.875
Were you guys... involved?

09:43.911 --> 09:45.143
We were, Peter.

09:45.179 --> 09:47.079
Korean O-M-G!

09:47.114 --> 09:48.747
Sujin, we actually
came here to find

09:48.782 --> 09:50.248
<i>the last episode
of Winter Summer.</i>

09:50.284 --> 09:51.516
Would you happen to have it?

09:51.552 --> 09:52.517
Of course.

09:52.553 --> 09:53.618
Can we see it?

09:53.654 --> 09:55.520
Why, yes.
Tonight.

09:55.556 --> 09:57.723
Glenn, you and your friends
must come to my home

09:57.758 --> 09:59.524
for gross
Korean dinner.

09:59.560 --> 10:00.659
Man, look at them.

10:00.694 --> 10:02.094
They make such
a cute couple.

10:02.129 --> 10:04.796
Like Pac-Man
and Ms. Pac-Man.

10:14.141 --> 10:17.175
I'm so happy you all
could make it tonight.

10:17.211 --> 10:19.578
We will have many things you
will nibble at and not eat.

10:19.613 --> 10:21.013
Then I will give
you a pizza.

10:21.048 --> 10:22.547
Yeah, yeah, yeah,
that's great.

10:22.583 --> 10:25.017
<i>Hey, can we watch that last
episode of Winter Summer now?</i>

10:25.052 --> 10:27.019
We will watch together
after dinner.

10:27.054 --> 10:30.255
In the meantime, feel free
to watch Korean pop videos.

10:43.237 --> 10:46.972
What is this, and how can I make
the rest of my life about it?

10:47.007 --> 10:48.407
Dinner will be
ready soon.

10:48.442 --> 10:50.842
But, Glenn, I have
a surprise for you.

10:50.878 --> 10:52.511
Do you remember
Buttercup?

10:52.546 --> 10:53.812
Who's Buttercup?

10:55.382 --> 10:58.216
Oh, my God, I can't believe
Buttercup is still alive!

10:58.252 --> 11:00.252
Alive and well.

11:00.287 --> 11:02.687
Wait a minute,
you named a cat Buttercup?

11:03.991 --> 11:05.857
Only Quagmire.

11:05.893 --> 11:08.060
And you know, Glenn,
after you moved away,

11:08.095 --> 11:09.528
Buttercup had kittens.

11:09.563 --> 11:10.796
What?

11:10.831 --> 11:11.863
That's right.

11:11.899 --> 11:13.565
You're a grandfather.

11:14.968 --> 11:16.835
My God.

11:16.870 --> 11:19.938
This is more pussy
than even I can handle.

11:19.973 --> 11:21.773
<i>Is he gonna say "giggity"?</i>

11:21.809 --> 11:23.275
<i>Should I say "giggity"?</i>

11:23.310 --> 11:26.044
<i>Are other people
allowed to say "giggity"?</i>

11:26.080 --> 11:27.145
Giggity.

11:27.181 --> 11:28.146
What?

11:28.182 --> 11:30.115
Nothing. It's stupid.

11:35.189 --> 11:37.556
Ah, that was a great
dinner, Sujin.

11:37.591 --> 11:38.957
I've missed you so much.

11:38.992 --> 11:41.626
I'd forgotten how happy
we make each other.

11:41.662 --> 11:43.562
Okay, I'm done
with this sweet rice water

11:43.597 --> 11:45.230
that has a pine nut
floating in it.

11:45.265 --> 11:46.431
Nice dessert,
by the way.

11:46.467 --> 11:47.632
Can we watch
the thing now?

11:47.668 --> 11:49.134
Of course.
Here it is--

11:49.169 --> 11:52.070
<i>the last episode
of Winter Summer.</i>

11:52.106 --> 11:53.106
Oh, my God!

11:53.140 --> 11:55.107
This is everything
I've dreamed of.

11:55.142 --> 11:58.143
Well, this, and becoming
a half-man, half-horse.

11:58.178 --> 12:00.078
Give up these legs?

12:00.114 --> 12:01.947
Don't be absurd.

12:30.811 --> 12:32.144
Why?!

12:32.179 --> 12:34.513
Why would American
Johnny leave Korea?

12:34.548 --> 12:36.281
He had everything!

12:36.316 --> 12:38.150
Love! A family!

12:38.185 --> 12:39.885
Why would he go
back to his sad,

12:39.920 --> 12:42.287
pathetic bachelor
life in America?!

12:42.322 --> 12:43.989
He's got nothing there!

12:44.024 --> 12:46.691
Why would he ever
want to go home?!

12:46.727 --> 12:48.326
Okay, Quagmire,
let's go home.

12:48.362 --> 12:50.128
Well, you know what?

12:50.164 --> 12:51.730
You're right, Peter.

12:51.765 --> 12:53.698
American Johnny
never should've left.

12:53.734 --> 12:56.101
It was the only time
he was ever happy.

12:56.136 --> 12:57.569
What? What are you saying?

12:57.604 --> 13:00.505
Hey, Sin-ju,
your TV says it's 21:00.

13:00.541 --> 13:02.340
What is that in real time?

13:02.376 --> 13:05.010
I'm saying I'm not going
back to Quahog.

13:05.045 --> 13:06.178
What?!

13:06.213 --> 13:07.946
But we've-we've
seen the last episode.

13:07.981 --> 13:09.648
We did what we came here to do.

13:09.683 --> 13:11.683
Peter, everything
you just said is true.

13:11.718 --> 13:13.919
I don't have anyone
waiting for me in Quahog.

13:13.954 --> 13:15.654
But here, I've got Sujin.

13:15.689 --> 13:18.056
I've got Buttercup
and our grandcats.

13:18.091 --> 13:19.457
I've got a family.

13:19.493 --> 13:22.727
I'm not gonna make the same
mistake American Johnny did.

13:22.763 --> 13:24.362
I'm staying here.

13:24.398 --> 13:27.899
<i>Will Quagmire stay in Korea?</i>

13:27.935 --> 13:30.101
<i>Will Peter find a new friend?</i>

13:30.137 --> 13:33.305
<i>Find out after this Korean
commercial Ashton Kutcher</i>

13:33.340 --> 13:37.042
<i>thought no one in America
would ever see.</i>

13:37.077 --> 13:39.077
Hi. I'm Ashton Kutcher.

13:39.112 --> 13:41.379
Have you ever killed a dog
while driving drunk,

13:41.415 --> 13:44.649
and then been upset that there
was no way for your car engine

13:44.685 --> 13:47.652
to cook it for you
on the rest of the drive home?

13:47.688 --> 13:49.187
Well, those days are over,

13:49.223 --> 13:52.457
thanks to Dr. Lee's
Pet Engine Cooking Bag.

13:52.492 --> 13:55.827
Just put the dog in the bag,
place it over the engine block,

13:55.862 --> 13:58.096
and drive your usual
20 miles per hour

13:58.131 --> 13:59.464
over the speed limit.

14:01.568 --> 14:04.035
Mmm. Bow-wow!

14:04.071 --> 14:05.604
I'm Ashton Kutcher,
and remember,

14:05.639 --> 14:08.006
Dr. Lee's Pet Engine
Cooking Bags

14:08.041 --> 14:10.075
are not meant for babies.

14:10.110 --> 14:12.110
But they can be used
for babies.

14:18.575 --> 14:20.208
Quagmire,
you can't stay in Korea.

14:20.243 --> 14:22.611
We all got lives back in Quahog.

14:22.646 --> 14:24.613
<i>That's just it, Peter--
you have lives.</i>

14:24.648 --> 14:26.681
You guys all have
wives and kids.

14:26.717 --> 14:29.050
And I have nothing
waiting for me back there.

14:29.086 --> 14:31.319
But here, I have a family.

14:31.355 --> 14:33.221
Plus, commercial pilots
around here can just

14:33.256 --> 14:35.590
fly their plane
into the ocean if they want.

14:35.626 --> 14:37.158
Peter's right--
we can't just leave you here.

14:37.194 --> 14:39.094
Who am I gonna get
all my wiener jokes from?

14:39.129 --> 14:40.595
You're my wiener guy.

14:40.631 --> 14:41.930
Joe, I got them from a book.

14:41.965 --> 14:43.598
I wish I didn't know that.

14:43.634 --> 14:45.967
Don't peek
behind the curtain, huh?

14:46.003 --> 14:48.136
Sorry, guys,
you're not gonna change my mind.

14:48.171 --> 14:51.573
I just feel like
I belong here with Sujin.

14:54.044 --> 14:55.310
What are you gonna do?

14:55.345 --> 14:57.212
It's a powerful thing
when a woman pays you

14:57.247 --> 14:59.280
even the slightest
bit of attention.

14:59.316 --> 15:01.583
Yeah, God knows
I've been there.

15:01.618 --> 15:02.684
Welcome to Chili's.

15:02.719 --> 15:04.119
We're through.

15:09.726 --> 15:12.160
Can't believe Quagmire
isn't coming back with us.

15:12.195 --> 15:14.696
Donna's mother?
It was suicide.

15:14.731 --> 15:17.198
You guys want to check out
Brazil while we're out?

15:17.234 --> 15:20.001
We just got to accept that
Quagmire has made his decision.

15:20.037 --> 15:21.870
There's nothing
